   "kind": "upstream",
   "summary": "<p>What the development is built on. <code>Statement.lean</code> imports only Mathlib, <code>Framework/</code> and <code>PhaseProduct/Statement.lean</code>: ForShor's gate language <code>LowGate</code>, its semantics classes (<code>QSemantics</code>, <code>LowerGateClass</code>), its resource model <code>shorGateResourceModel</code> (Cuccaro adders, arbitrary-angle rotations, not T), and the table language of <code>Framework/ToomCookTable.lean</code> (<code>Register</code>, <code>State</code>, <code>Point</code>, <code>valid_ops</code>, <code>Prog</code>, <code>run?</code>). The proofs may import more: ForShor's phase-product lemmas (<code>PhaseProduct/Proofs/</code>: the naive leaf, the basis-level gate laws, the register lemmas, the master theorem). Nothing in the order-finding development imports it: the only importers are <code>ForShor.lean</code> (the library root) and <code>Model/Standard/PhaseTripleProductHeadline.lean</code>.</p><p>The Statement imports: <code>Framework/AbstractMachine/Gates</code>, <code>Framework/AbstractMachine/LowGate</code>, <code>Framework/Gatecount/ResourceModel</code>, <code>Framework/Quantum/QSemantics</code>, <code>Framework/Quantum/Registers</code>, <code>Framework/Semantics/GateSemantics</code>, <code>Framework/Semantics/LowGateSemantics</code>, <code>Framework/ToomCookTable</code>, <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Statement</code>.</p><p>The proofs additionally import: <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Proofs/GateLaws</code>, <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Proofs/Math/MasterTheorem</code>, <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Proofs/Math/ToomCook</code>, <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Proofs/NaiveLeaf</code>, <code>Implementation/PhaseProduct/Proofs/Registers</code>.</p><p>The model headline imports: <code>Model/Standard/Lift</code>, <code>Model/Standard/LowGates</code>.</p>",
   "snippets": []
