   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">2 files · 53 declarations · 863 lines</p><p>The mathematics, before any gate. <code>node_identity</code> is the Toom–Cook identity for three factors, <code>evalPhase</code> the recursive semantics, <code>evalPhase_correct</code> (and the wrapping and exact-width variants) that the recursion computes \\(\\varphi\\,x_0x_1x_2\\).</p><p><code>Exact</code> replaces the scan by the <em>least</em> width that works, <code>ptpTightWidth</code> (defined in the Statement): it runs the program on coefficient rows, takes the largest demand on a signed register, and is proved sound, minimal and never larger than the scan.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/VerifiedQC/ForShor/blob/52a2c9eee41d/ForShor/ShorVerification/Implementation/PhaseTripleProduct/Proofs/Values/Semantics.lean\">Proofs/Values/Semantics.lean</a></td><td>9 decls</td><td>What a PTP policy computes: exact and wrapping-register semantics</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/VerifiedQC/ForShor/blob/52a2c9eee41d/ForShor/ShorVerification/Implementation/PhaseTripleProduct/Proofs/Values/Exact.lean\">Proofs/Values/Exact.lean</a></td><td>44 decls</td><td>Exact PTP widths (`ptpTightWidth`)</td></tr></table>",
