   "summary": "<p class=\"lmeta\">3 files · 85 declarations · 1,241 lines</p><p>One recursion level in ForShor's <code>LowGate</code>. The leaf and the node are defined in the Statement; this layer proves what they do. The node holds \\(3k\\) slot registers; each table operation becomes three gates, one per operand; the \\(t\\)-th <code>phaseProduct i</code> becomes a child on the triple <code>(slot 0 i, slot 1 i, slot 2 i)</code> at angle \\(\\varphi\\,c_t\\).</p><p>The base case is the sandwich leaf (<code>LeafSandwich</code>). <code>Leaf</code> keeps the earlier doubly-controlled-phase leaf as a documented alternative with all its theorems; no claim mentions it, so its definitions live in that proof file.</p><p><em>Not covered here:</em> splitting three parent registers into slots, reserve management, children that are themselves nodes, any controlled variant. Those are the next layers.</p><table class=\"ptp-mods\"><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/VerifiedQC/ForShor/blob/52a2c9eee41d/ForShor/ShorVerification/Implementation/PhaseTripleProduct/Proofs/Gates/Leaf.lean\">Proofs/Gates/Leaf.lean</a></td><td>26 decls</td><td>The PTP CCPhase leaf: a 3-way grid of doubly-controlled phases (gate level)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/VerifiedQC/ForShor/blob/52a2c9eee41d/ForShor/ShorVerification/Implementation/PhaseTripleProduct/Proofs/Gates/LeafSandwich.lean\">Proofs/Gates/LeafSandwich.lean</a></td><td>28 decls</td><td>The PTP sandwich leaf: compute–rotate–uncompute (gate level)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/VerifiedQC/ForShor/blob/52a2c9eee41d/ForShor/ShorVerification/Implementation/PhaseTripleProduct/Proofs/Gates/Node.lean\">Proofs/Gates/Node.lean</a></td><td>31 decls</td><td>One PTP recursion level at the gate level</td></tr></table>",
